{"strongs": "H3220", "word": "יָם", "translit": "yam", "root": "ימם", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "sea", "definition": "יָם 390 noun masculine Exod 14:27 sea (Phoenician ים ; Arabic ; Palmyrene בימא on the sea , Vog No. 79 ; on Assyrian iâmu, (¹mu) , sea , see Dl HWB 307 M-A CD 52 Hpt BAS i. 171 n .) — absolute יָם 1Sam 13:5 +; יָ֫מָּה Gen 28:14 +; construct יָם Gen 14:3 + 23 t., also יָ֫מָּה סוּף Exod 10:19 , but always יַםסֿוּף Exod 13:18 + 22 t.; suffix יַמָּהּ Jer 51:36 plural יַמִּים Judg 5:17 + 29 t.; — sea: especially 1. Mediterranean Num 13:29 ( E ), Num 34:5 ( P ), Deut 1:7 ; Josh 5:1 ; 1Kgs 5:23 (twice in verse); Jonah 1:4 (twice in verse) + often; the Mediterranean is called also הַיָּם הַגָּדוֺל Num 34:6 ; Num 34:7 ; Josh 15:12 ; Josh 15:47 ; Ezek 48:28 +, compare וּרְחַב יָדַיִם ׳ גּ ׳ הַיּ Ps 104:25 מְבוֺא ׳ הַיָּם חַגּ הַשָּׁ֑מֶשׁ Josh 1:4 ; Josh 23:4 (see Assyrian name of Mediterranean tiamtu rabitu ša sulmu šamši , etc., Schr Namender Meere. 171 ff. ); אֶלמֿוּל הַלְּבָנוֺן ׳ הַגּ ׳ הַיּ Josh 9:1 הָאַחֲרוֺן ׳ הַיּ the hinder sea Deut 11:24 ; Deut 34:2 ; Zech 14:8 ; Joel 2:20 (in the last two opposed to הַקַּדְמֹנִי ׳ הַיּ , see below); of Mediterranean in particular part יָם פְּלִשְׁתִּים Exod 23:31 ( J E ); יָם יָפוֺ 2Chr 2:15 = יָם יָפוֺא Ezra 3:7 . ** Of Mediterranean in plural Dan 11:45 [compare 8 d] Hi Ke Meinh Bev Dr (world-encircling seas Behrm). 2. יַםסֿוּף 'Red Sea' (see סוּף ) Exod 13:18 (compare Exod 10:19 ), Exod 15:4 ; Num 14:25 ; Deut 1:40 ; Josh 2:10 ; Judg 11:16 + often; also הַיָּם Exod 14:2 (twice in verse); Exod 14:9 ; Isa 51:10 (twice in verse); Isa 63:11 +; probably also יָםמִֿצְרַיִם Isa 11:15 'Red Sea' named or referred to approximately 66 t.; יִםסֿוּף clearly of lanitic Gulf 1Kgs 9:26 (compare 2Chr 8:17 ). 3. Dead Sea , יָם מֶלַח sea of salt Gen 14:3 ; Num 34:3 ; Num 34:12 ; Deut 3:17 ; Josh 3:16 ; Josh 12:3 ; Josh 15:2 ; Josh 15:5 ; Josh 18:19 יָם הָעֲרָבָה Deut 3:17 ; Deut 4:49 ; Josh 3:16 ; Josh 12:3 ; 2Kgs 14:25 הַקַּדְמֹנִי ׳ הַי Ezek 47:18 ; Zech 14:8 ; Joel 2:29 (see above); simply יָם Isa 16:8 ; Jer 48:32 — in יָם יַעְזֵר Jer 48:32 יָם is textual error, strike out with Gf Gr Che Gie . 4. Sea of Galilee יָם כִּנֶּרֶת Num 34:11 ; Josh 13:27 יָם כִּנְּרוֺת Josh 12:3 simply יָם Deut 33:23 . 5. more generally sea , opposed to earth and (or) sky Gen 1:26 ; Gen 1:28 ; Gen 9:2 ( P ), Exod 20:11 ( E ), Hag 2:6 + often Job, Psalms, Isa 2 etc.; Amos 6:12 read בַּבָּקָר יָם for בקרים (see בָּקָר ); sea as under earth Ps 24:2 (compare Gen 1:10 ; Gen 6:11 ; Exod 20:5 = Deut 5:3 ); figurative of flood of invaders, עָלָה עַלבָּֿבֶל הַיָּם Jer 51:42 . 6. of a mighty river , the Nile Nah 3:8 (twice in verse); Isa 19:5 (|| נָהָר ); compare הַתַּנִּין אֲשֶׁר בַּיָּם Isa 27:1 and כַּתַּנִּים בַּיַּמִּים Ezek 32:2 (simile of Pharaoh); of Euphrates Isa 21:1 ; Jer 51:36 (according to Che Gf and others; Isa 21:1 perhaps better of Persian Gulf, see Di ). 7. the great basin in temple-court, called the sea: וַיַּעַשׂ אֶתהַֿיָּם מוּצָק 1Kgs 7:23 = 2Chr 4:2 יָם הַנְּחשֶׁת 2Kgs 25:13 ; 1Chr 18:8 ; Jer 52:17 הַיָּם alone 1Kgs 7:24 ; 1Kgs 7:25 + 10 t. Kings Chronicles + Jer 52:20 . 8. combinations are: \\ \\ a. shore of sea, sea-shore שְׂפַת הַיָּם Josh 11:4 ; 1Kgs 5:9 , and in simile Gen 22:17 ; Judg 7:12 ; 1Sam 13:5 ׳ חוֺף הַי Josh 9:1 ; Ezek 25:16 חוֺף יַמִּים Gen 49:13 ; Judg 5:17 compare חֶבֶל הַיָּם Zeph 2:5 region by the sea ; so v Zeph 2:6 but dubious, see I. חֶבֶל 3. b. sand of the sea (shore) חוֺל הַיָּם (in simile) Gen 32:13 ; Gen 41:49 ; Hos 2:1 ; Isa 10:22 + often (see חוֺל ); חוֺל גְּבוּל לַיָּם Jer 5:22 . \\ \\ c. לְשׁוֺן הַיָּם tongue (arm or gulf) of sea Josh 15:5 ; Josh 18:19 ; Isa 11:5 . \\ \\ d. מִיָּם עַדיָֿם Amos 8:12 ; Zech 9:10 ; Ps 72:8 , compare Mic 7:12 ; Zech 14:8 (twice in verse); Joel 2:20 (twice in verse); Dan 11:45 . 9. = (west, west-word (originally sea-ward , from position of Mediterranean with reference to Palestine, and this sense still often perceptible): with other three points of compass Gen 13:14 ; Gen 28:14 ( J ), Num 2:18 ; Num 35:5 ( P ), Deut 3:27 ; 1Kgs 7:25 ; 1Chr 9:24 ; 2Chr 4:4 ; Ezek 42:19 + 6 t. Ezekiel; Zech 14:4 ; Dan 8:4 ; Ps 107:3 ( מִמִּזְרָח וּמִמַּעֲרָב מִצָּפוֺן וּמִיָּם ; but read perhaps וּמִיָּמִן from the south , Hu Pe Bi Che ); opposed to east Josh 11:2 ; Josh 16:6 + 16 t. Ezek 48 west alone Gen 12:8 ( J ); רוּהַ יָם Ezek 10:19 ( J ) west wind ; מִיָּם לְ westward Josh 8:9 ; Josh 8:12 ; Josh 8:13 +; יָ֫מָּה westward , often of tabernacle Exod 26:22 ; Exod 26:27 ; Num 3:23 + (all P ), and of land Josh 5:1 ; Josh 15:8 ; Josh 15:10 etc., + often Ezekiel; דֶּרֶךְ הַיָּם = westward Ezek 41:12 גְּבוּל יָם western border Num 34:6 (twice in verse); Josh 15:2 פְּאַתיָֿם west side Exod 27:12 ; Exod 38:12 ; Num 35:5 ; Josh 18:14 פְּאַת דרך הים Ezek 41:12 (see further פאה ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3567')\">BDB3567</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3220')\">H3220</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3566')\">BDB3566</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3568')\">BDB3568</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>יָם</bdbheb><sub>390</sub> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Exod 14:27\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(2,14,27)\">Exod 14:27</ref></sup> <highlightword>sea</highlightword> (Phoenician <bdbheb>ים</bdbheb>; Arabic <placeholder2229/>; Palmyrene <bdbheb>בימא</bdbheb> <highlight>on the sea</highlight>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Vog')\">Vog<sup>No. 79</sup></lookup>; on Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>iâmu, (¹mu)</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>sea</highlight>, see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dl')\">Dl<sup>HWB 307</sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('M-A')\">M-A<sup>CD 52</sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hpt')\">Hpt<sup>BAS i. 171 n</sup></lookup>.) — absolute <bdbheb>יָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Sam 13:5\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(9,13,5)\">1Sam 13:5</ref> +; <bdbheb>יָ֫מָּה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 28:14\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(1,28,14)\">Gen 28:14</ref> +; construct <bdbheb>יָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 14:3\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(1,14,3)\">Gen 14:3</ref> + 23 t., also <bdbheb>יָ֫מָּה סוּף</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 10:19\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(2,10,19)\">Exod 10:19</ref>, but always <bdbheb>יַםסֿוּף</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 13:18\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(2,13,18)\">Exod 13:18</ref> + 22 t.; suffix <bdbheb>יַמָּהּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 51:36\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"51\" vBegin=\"36\" cEnd=\"51\" vEnd=\"36\" onclick=\"bcv(24,51,36)\">Jer 51:36</ref> plural <bdbheb>יַמִּים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 5:17\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(7,5,17)\">Judg 5:17</ref> + 29 t.; — <highlight>sea:</highlight> especially <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>Mediterranean</highlight> <ref ref=\"Num 13:29\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(4,13,29)\">Num 13:29</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Num 34:5\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(4,34,5)\">Num 34:5</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Deut 1:7\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(5,1,7)\">Deut 1:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 5:1\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(6,5,1)\">Josh 5:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 5:23\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(11,5,23)\">1Kgs 5:23</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Jonah 1:4\" b=\"32\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(32,1,4)\">Jonah 1:4</ref> (twice in verse) + often; t